# Fundraising personalised name-sticker sample (D5)

## Product invariant

SELPIC sells **custom name stickers**. A sample is a **printed label with a nominated name**, shipped to the organisation contact address. There is **no generic blank Educator Sample Kit**.

- Default on apply: **do not request, do not ship**.
- Request only when the organisation ticks the optional box **and** enters a print name.
- Never hard-code `sampleKitRequested: false` while FAQ promises a kit, and never hard-code `true` on every application.
- Print name limit is `SAMPLE_STICKER_PRINT_NAME_MAX` (9) — same as `/stickers/customize` one-line names.
- Address + phone on the application are the delivery/contact details. Do not invent a separate sample-shipping form unless asked.
- Asking for a sample does **not** auto-dispatch. Admin still sends **D5** after review (`Dispatch personalised sample`).

## Surfaces

| Surface | Behaviour |
|---------|-----------|
| `/fundraising` apply | Optional checkbox + print-name field. FAQ matches this. |
| `POST /api/fundraising/apply` | `normalizeSampleKitRequest` — reject requested-without-name; ignore leftover name if unchecked. |
| D1 | Mentions the personalised request + print name only when requested. |
| D5 | Print name, ship-to address, contact. Warn if print name missing. |
| Admin Partners | Show requested/dispatched + print name. D5 option only when requested and not yet dispatched. |
| Lookup | No in-portal sample request yet. FAQ: email SELPIC after approval. |

## Do not

- Promise a complimentary generic kit in FAQ, D1, or landing copy
- Auto-flag every application as a sample request
- Put Etsy/cron or accounting-sandbox work into this flow
- Add partner self-serve bank PUT while touching this area
